PROVENANCE

The files in this directory and below it are the copy of the nofib benchmark suite (the collection
of Haskell programs that Will Partain gathered at Glasgow from many authors) that nhc98, a Haskell
98 compiler, keeps among its regression tests, tests/nofib in its repository. The CVS log kept in
real/grep/StringMatch.hs, lines 11 to 17, records the arrival of nhc98's tests, as revision 1.1 of
2004/08/05 by malcolm: "Add a regression testsuite for the nhc98 compiler.  It isn't very good, but
it is better than nothing. [...] It includes a slightly altered version of the nofib suite."

They are vendored here without a licence, under the rule of this repository's owner, quoted:

    "If you want to vendor code without a license add a PROVENANCE alongside it instead."

rhc, the Haskell 98 compiler of this repository, compiles and runs them in its tests
(tests/hs/corpus: the programs of D56 of the haskell98 roadmap, which tests/hs/corpus/licences.tsv
lists with this file as their notice).

Upstream
    repository  https://github.com/8l/nhc98.git
    commit      b4d41520ae51f1db61ff6fb899775200e4cae731, as tests/hs/corpus/trees.tsv pins it
    path        tests/nofib/ in that repository: a file at P below this directory
                is tests/nofib/P upstream
    fetched     2026-10-27, by git clone; the pinned commit was the head it fetched
    copied      2026-11-10, byte for byte, by `bin/rune-test hs-corpus-vendor`; the nightly test
                hs-corpus/vendored compares every file here with the pinned tree

Licence
    No licence is stated for these files. nofib states none, and nhc98's COPYRIGHT (at the root of
    its tree, not vendored) names what its licence covers: "the nhc98 Haskell compiler, libraries,
    and runtime system", and the tools hmake, hmake interactive, hmake-config and hp2graph; it does
    not name the tests. What notices single files carry is quoted below, program by program: gamteb
    and pic carry the Regents of the University of California's copyright and permission; multiplier
    its author's copyright, with no permission stated; boyer the Status "Public Domain" of its own
    header and of the header of the Scheme original it quotes; mandel the copyright line of the
    ppm(5) manual page it quotes.

Programs
    Each program by its id in tests/hs/corpus/candidates.tsv: its files, as paths below this
    directory; then what the files' own headers name of its authors and origin, and any notice,
    quoted as FILE:LINE and the line (tabs expanded, trailing blanks dropped). A program with no
    "named" names no author or origin in its files; one with no "notice" carries none.

